From 2a0ff070d544ad81c90b1d66979359af2f1e3194 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 12:56:25 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(skills): reasoning-driven skill auto-trigger (W1)

W1 makes Forge skills auto-trigger as a reasoning-driven SYSTEM (the owner's #1
complaint), not just harness description-matching. Four pieces:

1. NEW skills/using-forge/SKILL.md dispatch skill: 1%-rule, announce-before-acting,
   anti-rationalization red-flags table, subagent escape hatch, intent-to-skill
   routing table. Syncs to .agents/skills.
2. SessionStart injection: lib/commands/hooks.js injects the using-forge dispatch
   bootstrap FIRST (before the memory digest), the Superpowers mechanism; fail-open.
   The bash activation front-door (plugin/hooks/session-start) also names it.
3. forge prime live-state: prime leads with a bounded (<=20-line) block: stage,
   claimed issue(s), ready count, enabled gates/rails, and ONE adoption nudge.
   Best-effort, non-throwing, guards the non-repo path. Existing output unchanged.
4. NEW forge skill noun: forge skill for "<situation>" deterministic router with
   --json; reasoning fallback for harnesses without a SessionStart hook.

Naming/unification: EXTENDED forge prime (no forge orient dup); router under a NEW
forge skill noun, not a top-level forge which. Agent-agnostic: skill syncs to every
mirror and the CLI router works on any harness.

Kernel issues: using-forge-dispatch-skill-7c72c14b, forge-which-situation-deterministic-e606ea4e.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
